<article>
    <h1>{$selectedSection}</h1>
    <p>Given two vectors {`\\(\\vec{a}\\)`} and {`\\(\\vec{b}\\)`}, it is possible to subtract {`\\(\\vec{b}\\)`} <em>from</em> {`\\(\\vec{a}\\)`} and get a new vector written as {`\\(\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}\\)`}.</p>
    <p>To determine {`\\(\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}\\)`}, we write it as {`\\(\\vec{a} + (-\\vec{b})\\)`} which is just addition of vectors {`\\(\\vec{a}\\)`} and {`\\(-\\vec{b}\\)`}. We can apply either the <em>triangle law</em> or the <em>parallelogram law</em> of vector addition to get the sum. As noted in the previous section, {`\\(-\\vec{b}\\)`} is obtained by drawing {`\\(\\vec{b}\\)`} in the opposite direction keeping the <em>length</em> same.</p>
